bump this file to build the Mac test zip (.github/workflows/arpezator-mac.yml): ArpEZator alone, VST3 + AU + app, a workflow artifact, no public release
build 1: ArpEZator 3.2.0 - MUTANT ARP: the melodic sequence generator (RAGE / ALIEN / DIGITAL / DREAM / HYPER / FLUTE), chord-aware cells with octave jumps, pedals and pings, neighbour and chromatic approach notes, ratchets and 1/64 bursts, a variation every 2 / 4 bars, LOCK NOTES, MUTATE / OCTAVE CHAOS / RHYTHM CHAOS, EVOLVE 4 / 8 / 16, TWO LINES (ANSWER / INTERLOCK / SHADOW into the MELODY lane), 1/4..1/64, reverse / ping-pong / rotate, swing, glide, DRAG MIDI; older sessions and every old mood untouched
build 2: the MUTANT ARP button's tooltip names all six modes (FLUTE was missing); TWO_ANSWER and TWO_SHADOW demos; no engine change
build 3: ArpEZator 3.2.1 - the TRAP flute sings: DARK / TRIUMPHANT / HYPNOTIC / DRILL write slow trap-flute melodies measured from the flute reference (short phrases of 1/8s and 1/4s ending on long held notes with vibrato, breaths, mostly stepwise with one leap, repeated-note stabs, grace notes that scoop in, trills, slides; a 2-bar call that ends open and a 2-bar answer that lands; HYPNOTIC loops one bar); versioned per idea (melVer) so every session saved before 3.2.1 renders exactly as it did, GENERATE / a NEW melody take move it to the new writer. MUTANT ARP: FLUTE's button becomes CYBERPOP, a mode that generates from a style table learned from MIDI packs by tools/learn_pack.py (aggregate statistics only: onset grid, note lengths, interval histogram, accents, ratchets, repeat form; no phrases, no names); until the first pack is learned the table is a seed. FLUTE stays hidden for older sessions (bit-identical, fingerprint test). Old moods / TRAP / HIP HOP / Ghost Slice old sessions bit-identical; OLD MOODS constants re-baselined against pre-branch main.
build 4: ArpEZator 3.2.2 - CYBERPOP learned from the first MIDI pack set (3 lead tracks, 195 notes; aggregate statistics only): 8th-grid hooks at ~5 notes a bar in a one-octave band, the second bar answering the first; the register and MUTATE come from the table, CHORD FOLLOW keeps a hook's pitches over the chord loop (nudges beats onto the chord), the pitch walk has its own random stream; the no-copy check: 0 shared 4-note sequences with any lead track over 480 generated files. FLUTE (hidden) bit-identical; old moods, TRAP / HIP HOP and Ghost Slice old sessions untouched.
build 5: ArpEZator 3.2.2 - CYBERPOP retune: the learned table now includes the chord pad's top line (4 melodic tracks, 202 notes; drums / 808s left out); the move draw is smoothed with a generic prior and comes from the pitch walk's own stream (NOTE DENSITY no longer re-rolls the tune); a zigzag stair (the stock 4-note pop-hook figure) is broken on its 4th note; no-copy check over 1,920 files: 0 shared 5-note sequences with any melodic track, 4-note lead coincidences 4 in 1,200 CYBERPOP lines (generic 3-move shapes). FLUTE (hidden), old moods, saved sessions (the cell is stored) and Ghost Slice untouched.
